abstract: >-
  Scilab tool that simulates the negative electrode of a lead-acid battery: a system of differential-algebraic
  equations for the interfacial voltage, the porosity and the acid concentration across the thickness of the electrode,
  integrated by the DASSL solver of Scilab in dimensional or dimensionless form, for discharges at rates from 0.05C to
  12C followed by rests, compared with experimental records. It is a minimum working example for learning to model
  batteries and a framework for other primary and secondary technologies.
